node_modules/
.DS_Store
# Anchored to the root on purpose: tools/package.json and tools/package-lock.json
# ARE committed — the refresh workflow runs `npm ci` in tools/ and cannot install
# from a manifest that is not in the repository.
/package.json
/package-lock.json
_figtmp/
_*.png
tools/litro/
tools/figout/
tools/dump-*.json
# Frame dumps from tools/dump-frames.js — ~27 MB of regenerable intermediates
# between the screens and the .fig. Same reasoning as tools/dump-*.json above.
tools/dumps/

# Stakeholder comment dumps carry reviewer names and email addresses.
# Never commit them; they are private working files, not research.
comments/

# This repository is public and GitHub Pages serves it from `main`, so anything
# committed here is published under mateuszkoslacz.com. The review apparatus is
# not: `docs/audits/` carries the conversion analysis and the product owner's
# rulings, `docs/impl-guides/` carries every finding raised against the
# prototype, CLAUDE.md restates the conversion baseline and the funnel
# invariants, and `.review-lineage/` is the lifecycle graph over all of it.
# None of it had ever been pushed; keeping it untracked is the state this
# repository was already in, made explicit rather than left to chance.
# The prototype itself — screens, engines, review pages, the comment config
# the published site needs — stays committed.
docs/
CLAUDE.md
.review-lineage/
